<!-- The S.D. Tex. complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the
     typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 13 pt (Galveston Div. R. of Practice f and Judge Hanks Procs. 7.A;
     size 26 half points); Body Text in exact 26 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double, LR10.2 double spaced) with a
     half-inch indent, and the headings in them; the court title, caption and signature lines in 14.95 pt boxes (typst
     pitch-single); letter page with 1-inch margins. docx/txsd.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing, the page-number
     footer (its single-spaced line 35.45 pt above the page foot, 709 twips: where typst sets it, footer-descent 30 %)
     and the last section. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
